Aerie-Purpose: Put the tidy switches and the rename rules in the Sidebar section of Settings, let the settings page write their prefs, and add the "Try a title" message handler.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/resources/settings (appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.ts, appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.html.ts, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings (settings_localized_strings_provider.cc, settings_ui.cc, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private (prefs_util.cc)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #146. The element, settings-aerie-title-rules-row, is a Lit element in the overlay
(chrome/browser/resources/settings/appearance_page/aerie_title_rules_row.*): the switch of the
built-in tidy and its list of sites where it is off, the "All rename rules" switch, the rule list
(a listbox, reordered with Alt+Up and Alt+Down or the buttons) with its editor, and a "Try a
title" box. It writes four profile prefs registered by components/aerie_tab_model/tab_model_prefs.cc:
aerie.tabs.tidy_titles (boolean, on), aerie.tabs.tidy_off_sites (list), aerie.tabs.rename_rules_enabled
(boolean, on) and aerie.tabs.rename_rules (list). The names are string literals in the settings_private
allowlist, as for the other Aerie prefs, and a test compares them with the constants. The "Try a
title" box asks AerieTitleRulesHandler (overlay, chrome/browser/ui/webui/aerie_title_rules), a plain
message handler on chrome://settings only, which runs the real title resolver on the saved
settings. The strings are in the overlay's aerie_sidebar_strings.grdp, which patches/sidebar/0022
includes in generated_resources.grd; this patch hands them to the page. The element sits last in
the "Sidebar" section.

--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
@@ -502,6 +502,15 @@
   // The name is aerie_tab_model::kFolderRulesEnabled; a test compares the two.
   (*s_allowlist)["aerie.folders.rules_enabled"] =
       settings_api::PrefType::kBoolean;
+  // Aerie: the tidy of tab titles and the rename rules (issue #146). The names
+  // are aerie_tab_model::kTidyTitles, kTidyOffSites, kRenameRulesEnabled and
+  // kRenameRules; a test compares them. The rules are untrusted when they are
+  // read (components/aerie_tab_model/rename_rules.cc).
+  (*s_allowlist)["aerie.tabs.tidy_titles"] = settings_api::PrefType::kBoolean;
+  (*s_allowlist)["aerie.tabs.tidy_off_sites"] = settings_api::PrefType::kList;
+  (*s_allowlist)["aerie.tabs.rename_rules_enabled"] =
+      settings_api::PrefType::kBoolean;
+  (*s_allowlist)["aerie.tabs.rename_rules"] = settings_api::PrefType::kList;
   // Aerie: the sidebar's density and side (issue #184). The names are
   // aerie_sidebar::kDensityPref and kSidePref; a test compares them.
   (*s_allowlist)["aerie.sidebar.density"] = settings_api::PrefType::kString;
